{"track":"est2","num":"5.01","title":"Trigonometry","sections":[{"heading":"The unit circle and radian measure","questions":[{"q":"Convert $210^\\circ$ to radians.","answer":"$210\\times\\dfrac{\\pi}{180}=\\dfrac{7\\pi}{6}$."},{"q":"Convert $\\dfrac{5\\pi}{4}$ radians to degrees.","answer":"$\\dfrac{5\\pi}{4}\\times\\dfrac{180}{\\pi}=225^\\circ$."},{"q":"Find the exact value of $\\sin(240^\\circ)$.","answer":"$240^\\circ$ is in Quadrant III with reference angle $60^\\circ$, where sine is negative: $\\sin(240^\\circ)=-\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$."}]},{"heading":"Trigonometric identities","questions":[{"q":"Simplify $\\dfrac{1-\\sin^2\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}$.","answer":"$\\dfrac{\\cos^2\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}=\\cos\\theta$."},{"q":"Simplify $\\tan\\theta\\cdot\\cos\\theta$.","answer":"$\\dfrac{\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}\\cdot\\cos\\theta=\\sin\\theta$."},{"q":"If $\\sin\\theta=\\dfrac{3}{5}$ and $\\theta$ is in Quadrant II, find $\\cos\\theta$ and $\\tan\\theta$.","answer":"$\\cos\\theta=-\\sqrt{1-\\dfrac{9}{25}}=-\\dfrac{4}{5}$ (negative in Quadrant II). $\\tan\\theta=\\dfrac{\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}=\\dfrac{3/5}{-4/5}=-\\dfrac{3}{4}$."}]},{"heading":"Double angle formulas","questions":[{"q":"Given $\\cos\\theta=\\dfrac{5}{13}$ with $\\theta$ in Quadrant I, find $\\sin2\\theta$ and $\\cos2\\theta$.","answer":"$\\sin\\theta=\\sqrt{1-\\dfrac{25}{169}}=\\dfrac{12}{13}$. $\\sin2\\theta=2\\left(\\dfrac{12}{13}\\right)\\left(\\dfrac{5}{13}\\right)=\\dfrac{120}{169}$. $\\cos2\\theta=1-2\\sin^2\\theta=1-\\dfrac{288}{169}=-\\dfrac{119}{169}$."},{"q":"Use double-angle formulas to express $\\sin4\\theta$ in terms of $\\sin\\theta$ and $\\cos\\theta$ only.","answer":"$\\sin4\\theta=2\\sin2\\theta\\cos2\\theta=2(2\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta)(1-2\\sin^2\\theta)=4\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta(1-2\\sin^2\\theta)$."}]},{"heading":"Solving trigonometric equations","questions":[{"q":"Solve $2\\sin\\theta-1=0$ for $0^\\circ\\leq\\theta<360^\\circ$.","answer":"$\\sin\\theta=\\dfrac{1}{2}\\Rightarrow\\theta=30^\\circ$ or $\\theta=150^\\circ$."},{"q":"Solve $2\\cos^2\\theta+\\cos\\theta-1=0$ for $0^\\circ\\leq\\theta<360^\\circ$.","answer":"Factoring: $(2\\cos\\theta-1)(\\cos\\theta+1)=0$. $\\cos\\theta=\\dfrac{1}{2}\\Rightarrow\\theta=60^\\circ,300^\\circ$. $\\cos\\theta=-1\\Rightarrow\\theta=180^\\circ$. Solutions: $60^\\circ,180^\\circ,300^\\circ$."}]},{"heading":"Graphs of trigonometric functions","questions":[{"q":"The graph shows $y=3\\sin(2x)$. State the amplitude and period.","figure":{"type":"plot","fns":["3*sin(2*x)"],"xmin":-4,"xmax":4,"ymin":-4,"ymax":4,"width":220},"answer":"Amplitude $=3$. Period $=\\dfrac{2\\pi}{2}=\\pi$."},{"q":"The function $y=4\\cos(3x-\\pi)$ has what amplitude, period, and phase shift?","answer":"Amplitude $=4$. Period $=\\dfrac{2\\pi}{3}$. Writing $3x-\\pi=3\\left(x-\\dfrac{\\pi}{3}\\right)$, the phase shift is $\\dfrac{\\pi}{3}$ to the right."}]},{"heading":"The Law of Sines","questions":[{"q":"In triangle $ABC$, $a=10$, $A=40^\\circ$, $B=65^\\circ$. Find $b$, to the nearest hundredth.","answer":"$\\dfrac{b}{\\sin B}=\\dfrac{a}{\\sin A}\\Rightarrow b=\\dfrac{10\\sin65^\\circ}{\\sin40^\\circ}\\approx\\dfrac{9.063}{0.643}\\approx14.10$."},{"q":"In triangle $ABC$, $a=8$, $b=10$, $A=35^\\circ$. Determine how many triangles are possible, and find angle $B$ (to the nearest tenth of a degree) for each.","answer":"$h=b\\sin A=10\\sin35^\\circ\\approx5.74$. Since $h<a<b$, two triangles are possible. $\\sin B=\\dfrac{b\\sin A}{a}\\approx0.717\\Rightarrow B\\approx45.8^\\circ$ or $B\\approx180^\\circ-45.8^\\circ=134.2^\\circ$. Both are valid since $A+B<180^\\circ$ in each case."}]},{"heading":"The Law of Cosines and the sine area formula","questions":[{"q":"In triangle $ABC$ shown below, $a=11$, $b=14$, and $C=55^\\circ$. Find side $c$, to the nearest hundredth, and the area of the triangle, to the nearest tenth.","figure":{"type":"triangle","vertices":[[0,0],[10,0],[4,7]],"labels":["A","B","C"],"side_labels":["c","11","14"],"angle_marks":[{"vertex":2,"label":"55°"}],"width":200},"answer":"$c^2=11^2+14^2-2(11)(14)\\cos55^\\circ\\approx317-176.66=140.34$, so $c\\approx11.85$. Area $=\\dfrac{1}{2}(11)(14)\\sin55^\\circ=77\\sin55^\\circ\\approx63.1$."},{"q":"State the two formulas used above (Law of Cosines for a side, and the sine formula for area) in general form for a triangle with sides $a$, $b$, $c$ and included angle $C$.","answer":"Law of Cosines: $c^2=a^2+b^2-2ab\\cos C$. Area $=\\dfrac{1}{2}ab\\sin C$."}]},{"heading":"Inverse trigonometric functions","questions":[{"q":"Evaluate $\\arcsin\\left(\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)$ exactly, in radians.","answer":"$\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}$."},{"q":"Evaluate $\\arccos(-1)$ exactly, in radians.","answer":"$\\pi$."},{"q":"Find $\\theta=\\arctan(1)$ in degrees (principal value).","answer":"$45^\\circ$."}]},{"heading":"A well-designed word problem: locating a ship from two lighthouses","questions":[{"q":"This question has three parts. Two lighthouses $A$ and $B$ are $15$ km apart along a straight coastline. A ship at point $C$ is sighted such that $\\angle CAB=72^\\circ$ and $\\angle CBA=58^\\circ$ (both measured from line $AB$ toward the ship). (a) Find $\\angle ACB$. (b) Use the Law of Sines to find the distance $AC$ from lighthouse $A$ to the ship, to the nearest tenth of a km. (c) Find the distance $BC$ from lighthouse $B$ to the ship, to the nearest tenth of a km.","answer":"(a) $\\angle ACB=180^\\circ-72^\\circ-58^\\circ=50^\\circ$. (b) $AC$ is opposite $\\angle B$: $AC=\\dfrac{AB\\sin B}{\\sin C}=\\dfrac{15\\sin58^\\circ}{\\sin50^\\circ}\\approx16.6$ km. (c) $BC$ is opposite $\\angle A$: $BC=\\dfrac{AB\\sin A}{\\sin C}=\\dfrac{15\\sin72^\\circ}{\\sin50^\\circ}\\approx18.6$ km."}]},{"heading":"Multiple choice — easy","questions":[{"q":"Convert $135^\\circ$ to radians.","choices":["$\\dfrac{3\\pi}{5}$","$\\dfrac{3\\pi}{2}$","$\\dfrac{3\\pi}{4}$","$\\pi$"],"correct":2,"answer":"$135\\times\\dfrac{\\pi}{180}=\\dfrac{3\\pi}{4}$."},{"q":"Convert $60^\\circ$ to radians.","choices":["$\\dfrac{2\\pi}{3}$","$\\pi$","$\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}$","$\\dfrac{\\pi}{3}$"],"correct":3,"answer":"$60\\times\\dfrac{\\pi}{180}=\\dfrac{\\pi}{3}$."},{"q":"Convert $345^\\circ$ to radians.","choices":["$2\\pi$","$\\dfrac{23\\pi}{13}$","$\\dfrac{23\\pi}{12}$","$\\dfrac{23\\pi}{6}$"],"correct":2,"answer":"$345\\times\\dfrac{\\pi}{180}=\\dfrac{23\\pi}{12}$."},{"q":"Convert $105^\\circ$ to radians.","choices":["$\\dfrac{2\\pi}{3}$","$\\dfrac{7\\pi}{13}$","$\\dfrac{7\\pi}{6}$","$\\dfrac{7\\pi}{12}$"],"correct":3,"answer":"$105\\times\\dfrac{\\pi}{180}=\\dfrac{7\\pi}{12}$."},{"q":"Convert $90^\\circ$ to radians.","choices":["$\\pi$","$\\dfrac{3\\pi}{2}$","$\\dfrac{\\pi}{3}$","$\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}$"],"correct":3,"answer":"$90\\times\\dfrac{\\pi}{180}=\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}$."},{"q":"Convert $30^\\circ$ to radians.","choices":["$\\dfrac{\\pi}{3}$","$\\dfrac{\\pi}{7}$","$\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}$","$\\dfrac{\\pi}{6}$"],"correct":3,"answer":"$30\\times\\dfrac{\\pi}{180}=\\dfrac{\\pi}{6}$."},{"q":"Convert $315^\\circ$ to radians.","choices":["$\\dfrac{7\\pi}{5}$","$\\dfrac{7\\pi}{2}$","$2\\pi$","$\\dfrac{7\\pi}{4}$"],"correct":3,"answer":"$315\\times\\dfrac{\\pi}{180}=\\dfrac{7\\pi}{4}$."},{"q":"Convert $45^\\circ$ to radians.","choices":["$\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}$","$\\dfrac{\\pi}{5}$","$\\dfrac{3\\pi}{4}$","$\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}$"],"correct":0,"answer":"$45\\times\\dfrac{\\pi}{180}=\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}$."},{"q":"Convert $165^\\circ$ to radians.","choices":["$\\dfrac{11\\pi}{6}$","$\\dfrac{11\\pi}{12}$","$\\pi$","$\\dfrac{11\\pi}{13}$"],"correct":1,"answer":"$165\\times\\dfrac{\\pi}{180}=\\dfrac{11\\pi}{12}$."},{"q":"Convert $225^\\circ$ to radians.","choices":["$\\dfrac{5\\pi}{2}$","$\\dfrac{5\\pi}{4}$","$\\pi$","$\\dfrac{3\\pi}{2}$"],"correct":1,"answer":"$225\\times\\dfrac{\\pi}{180}=\\dfrac{5\\pi}{4}$."},{"q":"Convert $150^\\circ$ to radians.","choices":["$\\dfrac{5\\pi}{7}$","$\\dfrac{5\\pi}{3}$","$\\pi$","$\\dfrac{5\\pi}{6}$"],"correct":3,"answer":"$150\\times\\dfrac{\\pi}{180}=\\dfrac{5\\pi}{6}$."},{"q":"Convert $15^\\circ$ to radians.","choices":["$\\dfrac{\\pi}{6}$","$\\dfrac{\\pi}{13}$","$\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}$","$\\dfrac{\\pi}{12}$"],"correct":3,"answer":"$15\\times\\dfrac{\\pi}{180}=\\dfrac{\\pi}{12}$."},{"q":"Convert $75^\\circ$ to radians.","choices":["$\\dfrac{5\\pi}{12}$","$\\dfrac{5\\pi}{13}$","$\\dfrac{5\\pi}{6}$","$\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}$"],"correct":0,"answer":"$75\\times\\dfrac{\\pi}{180}=\\dfrac{5\\pi}{12}$."},{"q":"Convert $210^\\circ$ to radians.","choices":["$\\pi$","$\\dfrac{4\\pi}{3}$","$\\dfrac{7\\pi}{3}$","$\\dfrac{7\\pi}{6}$"],"correct":3,"answer":"$210\\times\\dfrac{\\pi}{180}=\\dfrac{7\\pi}{6}$."},{"q":"Convert $240^\\circ$ to radians.","choices":["$\\dfrac{5\\pi}{3}$","$\\dfrac{4\\pi}{3}$","$\\pi$","$\\dfrac{8\\pi}{3}$"],"correct":1,"answer":"$240\\times\\dfrac{\\pi}{180}=\\dfrac{4\\pi}{3}$."}]},{"heading":"Multiple choice — medium","questions":[{"q":"Solve $\\tan\\theta=-1$ for $0^\\circ\\leq\\theta<360^\\circ$.","choices":["$120^\\circ,300^\\circ$","$45^\\circ,225^\\circ$","$30^\\circ,210^\\circ$","$135^\\circ,315^\\circ$"],"correct":3,"answer":"$\\tan\\theta=-1\\Rightarrow\\theta=135^\\circ$ or $\\theta=315^\\circ$."},{"q":"Solve $\\tan\\theta=-\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}$ for $0^\\circ\\leq\\theta<360^\\circ$.","choices":["$30^\\circ,210^\\circ$","$150^\\circ,330^\\circ$","$135^\\circ,315^\\circ$","$120^\\circ,300^\\circ$"],"correct":1,"answer":"$\\tan\\theta=-\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\Rightarrow\\theta=150^\\circ$ or $\\theta=330^\\circ$."},{"q":"Solve $\\tan\\theta=-\\sqrt{3}$ for $0^\\circ\\leq\\theta<360^\\circ$.","choices":["$150^\\circ,330^\\circ$","$120^\\circ,300^\\circ$","$135^\\circ,315^\\circ$","$60^\\circ,240^\\circ$"],"correct":1,"answer":"$\\tan\\theta=-\\sqrt{3}\\Rightarrow\\theta=120^\\circ$ or $\\theta=300^\\circ$."},{"q":"Solve $\\sin\\theta=-\\dfrac{1}{2}$ for $0^\\circ\\leq\\theta<360^\\circ$.","choices":["$225^\\circ,315^\\circ$","$210^\\circ,330^\\circ$","$30^\\circ,150^\\circ$","$45^\\circ,135^\\circ$"],"correct":1,"answer":"$\\sin\\theta=-\\dfrac{1}{2}\\Rightarrow\\theta=210^\\circ$ or $\\theta=330^\\circ$."},{"q":"Solve $\\cos\\theta=-\\dfrac{1}{2}$ for $0^\\circ\\leq\\theta<360^\\circ$.","choices":["$30^\\circ,330^\\circ$","$135^\\circ,225^\\circ$","$150^\\circ,210^\\circ$","$120^\\circ,240^\\circ$"],"correct":3,"answer":"$\\cos\\theta=-\\dfrac{1}{2}\\Rightarrow\\theta=120^\\circ$ or $\\theta=240^\\circ$."},{"q":"Solve $\\cos\\theta=\\dfrac{1}{2}$ for $0^\\circ\\leq\\theta<360^\\circ$.","choices":["$135^\\circ,225^\\circ$","$150^\\circ,210^\\circ$","$45^\\circ,315^\\circ$","$60^\\circ,300^\\circ$"],"correct":3,"answer":"$\\cos\\theta=\\dfrac{1}{2}\\Rightarrow\\theta=60^\\circ$ or $\\theta=300^\\circ$."},{"q":"Solve $\\cos\\theta=\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ for $0^\\circ\\leq\\theta<360^\\circ$.","choices":["$135^\\circ,225^\\circ$","$30^\\circ,330^\\circ$","$120^\\circ,240^\\circ$","$60^\\circ,300^\\circ$"],"correct":1,"answer":"$\\cos\\theta=\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\Rightarrow\\theta=30^\\circ$ or $\\theta=330^\\circ$."},{"q":"Solve $\\cos\\theta=\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ for $0^\\circ\\leq\\theta<360^\\circ$.","choices":["$150^\\circ,210^\\circ$","$30^\\circ,330^\\circ$","$45^\\circ,315^\\circ$","$120^\\circ,240^\\circ$"],"correct":2,"answer":"$\\cos\\theta=\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\Rightarrow\\theta=45^\\circ$ or $\\theta=315^\\circ$."},{"q":"Solve $\\sin\\theta=\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ for $0^\\circ\\leq\\theta<360^\\circ$.","choices":["$30^\\circ,150^\\circ$","$240^\\circ,300^\\circ$","$60^\\circ,120^\\circ$","$210^\\circ,330^\\circ$"],"correct":2,"answer":"$\\sin\\theta=\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\Rightarrow\\theta=60^\\circ$ or $\\theta=120^\\circ$."},{"q":"Solve $\\tan\\theta=\\sqrt{3}$ for $0^\\circ\\leq\\theta<360^\\circ$.","choices":["$60^\\circ,240^\\circ$","$135^\\circ,315^\\circ$","$150^\\circ,330^\\circ$","$120^\\circ,300^\\circ$"],"correct":0,"answer":"$\\tan\\theta=\\sqrt{3}\\Rightarrow\\theta=60^\\circ$ or $\\theta=240^\\circ$."},{"q":"Solve $\\tan\\theta=\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}$ for $0^\\circ\\leq\\theta<360^\\circ$.","choices":["$120^\\circ,300^\\circ$","$30^\\circ,210^\\circ$","$135^\\circ,315^\\circ$","$60^\\circ,240^\\circ$"],"correct":1,"answer":"$\\tan\\theta=\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\Rightarrow\\theta=30^\\circ$ or $\\theta=210^\\circ$."},{"q":"Solve $\\tan\\theta=1$ for $0^\\circ\\leq\\theta<360^\\circ$.","choices":["$60^\\circ,240^\\circ$","$120^\\circ,300^\\circ$","$45^\\circ,225^\\circ$","$150^\\circ,330^\\circ$"],"correct":2,"answer":"$\\tan\\theta=1\\Rightarrow\\theta=45^\\circ$ or $\\theta=225^\\circ$."},{"q":"Solve $\\sin\\theta=-\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ for $0^\\circ\\leq\\theta<360^\\circ$.","choices":["$210^\\circ,330^\\circ$","$240^\\circ,300^\\circ$","$225^\\circ,315^\\circ$","$60^\\circ,120^\\circ$"],"correct":1,"answer":"$\\sin\\theta=-\\dfrac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\Rightarrow\\theta=240^\\circ$ or $\\theta=300^\\circ$."},{"q":"Solve $\\sin\\theta=\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ for $0^\\circ\\leq\\theta<360^\\circ$.","choices":["$60^\\circ,120^\\circ$","$30^\\circ,150^\\circ$","$45^\\circ,135^\\circ$","$240^\\circ,300^\\circ$"],"correct":2,"answer":"$\\sin\\theta=\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\Rightarrow\\theta=45^\\circ$ or $\\theta=135^\\circ$."},{"q":"Solve $\\sin\\theta=-\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ for $0^\\circ\\leq\\theta<360^\\circ$.","choices":["$210^\\circ,330^\\circ$","$45^\\circ,135^\\circ$","$60^\\circ,120^\\circ$","$225^\\circ,315^\\circ$"],"correct":3,"answer":"$\\sin\\theta=-\\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\Rightarrow\\theta=225^\\circ$ or $\\theta=315^\\circ$."}]},{"heading":"Multiple choice — hard","questions":[{"q":"In triangle $ABC$, $a=18$, $A=80^\\circ$, $B=70^\\circ$. Find $b$, to the nearest hundredth.","choices":["$17.68$","$18.18$","$17.18$","$16.68$"],"correct":2,"answer":"$\\dfrac{b}{\\sin B}=\\dfrac{a}{\\sin A}\\Rightarrow b=\\dfrac{18\\sin70^\\circ}{\\sin80^\\circ}\\approx\\dfrac{16.914}{0.985}\\approx17.18$."},{"q":"In triangle $ABC$, $a=17$, $A=20^\\circ$, $B=80^\\circ$. Find $b$, to the nearest hundredth.","choices":["$48.95$","$49.95$","$49.45$","$48.45$"],"correct":0,"answer":"$\\dfrac{b}{\\sin B}=\\dfrac{a}{\\sin A}\\Rightarrow b=\\dfrac{17\\sin80^\\circ}{\\sin20^\\circ}\\approx\\dfrac{16.742}{0.342}\\approx48.95$."},{"q":"In triangle $ABC$, $a=15$, $A=60^\\circ$, $B=30^\\circ$. Find $b$, to the nearest hundredth.","choices":["$9.16$","$8.66$","$8.16$","$9.66$"],"correct":1,"answer":"$\\dfrac{b}{\\sin B}=\\dfrac{a}{\\sin A}\\Rightarrow b=\\dfrac{15\\sin30^\\circ}{\\sin60^\\circ}\\approx\\dfrac{7.500}{0.866}\\approx8.66$."},{"q":"In triangle $ABC$, $a=11$, $A=55^\\circ$, $B=60^\\circ$. Find $b$, to the nearest hundredth.","choices":["$11.13$","$12.13$","$12.63$","$11.63$"],"correct":3,"answer":"$\\dfrac{b}{\\sin B}=\\dfrac{a}{\\sin A}\\Rightarrow b=\\dfrac{11\\sin60^\\circ}{\\sin55^\\circ}\\approx\\dfrac{9.526}{0.819}\\approx11.63$."},{"q":"In triangle $ABC$, $a=17$, $A=80^\\circ$, $B=45^\\circ$. Find $b$, to the nearest hundredth.","choices":["$12.71$","$12.21$","$13.21$","$11.71$"],"correct":1,"answer":"$\\dfrac{b}{\\sin B}=\\dfrac{a}{\\sin A}\\Rightarrow b=\\dfrac{17\\sin45^\\circ}{\\sin80^\\circ}\\approx\\dfrac{12.021}{0.985}\\approx12.21$."},{"q":"In triangle $ABC$, $a=9$, $b=15$, and $C=110^\\circ$. Find side $c$, to the nearest hundredth, and the area, to the nearest tenth.","choices":["$18.96,61.4$","$19.96,65.4$","$20.96,63.4$","$19.96,63.4$"],"correct":3,"answer":"$c^2=9^2+15^2-2(9)(15)\\cos110^\\circ\\approx306+92.35\\approx398.35$, so $c\\approx19.96$. Area $=\\dfrac{1}{2}(9)(15)\\sin110^\\circ=\\dfrac{135}{2}\\sin110^\\circ\\approx63.4$."},{"q":"In triangle $ABC$, $a=13$, $b=11$, and $C=130^\\circ$. Find side $c$, to the nearest hundredth, and the area, to the nearest tenth.","choices":["$21.77,56.8$","$21.77,54.8$","$20.77,52.8$","$22.77,54.8$"],"correct":1,"answer":"$c^2=13^2+11^2-2(13)(11)\\cos130^\\circ\\approx290+183.84\\approx473.84$, so $c\\approx21.77$. Area $=\\dfrac{1}{2}(13)(11)\\sin130^\\circ=\\dfrac{143}{2}\\sin130^\\circ\\approx54.8$."},{"q":"In triangle $ABC$, $a=13$, $b=9$, and $C=80^\\circ$. Find side $c$, to the nearest hundredth, and the area, to the nearest tenth.","choices":["$14.47,57.6$","$15.47,57.6$","$14.47,59.6$","$13.47,55.6$"],"correct":0,"answer":"$c^2=13^2+9^2-2(13)(9)\\cos80^\\circ\\approx250-40.63\\approx209.37$, so $c\\approx14.47$. Area $=\\dfrac{1}{2}(13)(9)\\sin80^\\circ=\\dfrac{117}{2}\\sin80^\\circ\\approx57.6$."},{"q":"In triangle $ABC$, $a=14$, $b=10$, and $C=60^\\circ$. Find side $c$, to the nearest hundredth, and the area, to the nearest tenth.","choices":["$12.49,60.6$","$13.49,60.6$","$12.49,62.6$","$11.49,58.6$"],"correct":0,"answer":"$c^2=14^2+10^2-2(14)(10)\\cos60^\\circ\\approx296-140.00\\approx156.00$, so $c\\approx12.49$. Area $=\\dfrac{1}{2}(14)(10)\\sin60^\\circ=70\\sin60^\\circ\\approx60.6$."},{"q":"In triangle $ABC$, $a=9$, $b=12$, and $C=70^\\circ$. Find side $c$, to the nearest hundredth, and the area, to the nearest tenth.","choices":["$12.29,52.7$","$11.29,48.7$","$13.29,50.7$","$12.29,50.7$"],"correct":3,"answer":"$c^2=9^2+12^2-2(9)(12)\\cos70^\\circ\\approx225-73.88\\approx151.12$, so $c\\approx12.29$. Area $=\\dfrac{1}{2}(9)(12)\\sin70^\\circ=54\\sin70^\\circ\\approx50.7$."},{"q":"Given $\\cos\\theta=\\dfrac{35}{37}$ with $\\theta$ in Quadrant I, find $\\sin2\\theta$ and $\\cos2\\theta$.","choices":["$\\dfrac{840}{1369},\\dfrac{1081}{1369}$","$\\dfrac{840}{1369},-\\dfrac{1081}{1369}$","$-\\dfrac{840}{1369},\\dfrac{1081}{1369}$","$\\dfrac{1081}{1369},\\dfrac{840}{1369}$"],"correct":0,"answer":"$\\sin\\theta=\\sqrt{1-\\dfrac{1225}{1369}}=\\dfrac{12}{37}$. $\\sin2\\theta=2\\left(\\dfrac{12}{37}\\right)\\left(\\dfrac{35}{37}\\right)=\\dfrac{840}{1369}$. $\\cos2\\theta=1-2\\sin^2\\theta=1-\\dfrac{288}{1369}=\\dfrac{1081}{1369}$."},{"q":"Given $\\cos\\theta=\\dfrac{24}{25}$ with $\\theta$ in Quadrant I, find $\\sin2\\theta$ and $\\cos2\\theta$.","choices":["$-\\dfrac{336}{625},\\dfrac{527}{625}$","$\\dfrac{336}{625},\\dfrac{527}{625}$","$\\dfrac{336}{625},-\\dfrac{527}{625}$","$\\dfrac{527}{625},\\dfrac{336}{625}$"],"correct":1,"answer":"$\\sin\\theta=\\sqrt{1-\\dfrac{576}{625}}=\\dfrac{7}{25}$. $\\sin2\\theta=2\\left(\\dfrac{7}{25}\\right)\\left(\\dfrac{24}{25}\\right)=\\dfrac{336}{625}$. $\\cos2\\theta=1-2\\sin^2\\theta=1-\\dfrac{98}{625}=\\dfrac{527}{625}$."},{"q":"Given $\\cos\\theta=\\dfrac{15}{17}$ with $\\theta$ in Quadrant I, find $\\sin2\\theta$ and $\\cos2\\theta$.","choices":["$\\dfrac{240}{289},-\\dfrac{161}{289}$","$-\\dfrac{240}{289},\\dfrac{161}{289}$","$\\dfrac{240}{289},\\dfrac{161}{289}$","$\\dfrac{161}{289},\\dfrac{240}{289}$"],"correct":2,"answer":"$\\sin\\theta=\\sqrt{1-\\dfrac{225}{289}}=\\dfrac{8}{17}$. $\\sin2\\theta=2\\left(\\dfrac{8}{17}\\right)\\left(\\dfrac{15}{17}\\right)=\\dfrac{240}{289}$. $\\cos2\\theta=1-2\\sin^2\\theta=1-\\dfrac{128}{289}=\\dfrac{161}{289}$."},{"q":"Given $\\cos\\theta=\\dfrac{12}{13}$ with $\\theta$ in Quadrant I, find $\\sin2\\theta$ and $\\cos2\\theta$.","choices":["$-\\dfrac{120}{169},\\dfrac{119}{169}$","$\\dfrac{120}{169},-\\dfrac{119}{169}$","$\\dfrac{119}{169},\\dfrac{120}{169}$","$\\dfrac{120}{169},\\dfrac{119}{169}$"],"correct":3,"answer":"$\\sin\\theta=\\sqrt{1-\\dfrac{144}{169}}=\\dfrac{5}{13}$. $\\sin2\\theta=2\\left(\\dfrac{5}{13}\\right)\\left(\\dfrac{12}{13}\\right)=\\dfrac{120}{169}$. $\\cos2\\theta=1-2\\sin^2\\theta=1-\\dfrac{50}{169}=\\dfrac{119}{169}$."},{"q":"Given $\\cos\\theta=\\dfrac{4}{5}$ with $\\theta$ in Quadrant I, find $\\sin2\\theta$ and $\\cos2\\theta$.","choices":["$-\\dfrac{24}{25},\\dfrac{7}{25}$","$\\dfrac{24}{25},\\dfrac{7}{25}$","$\\dfrac{24}{25},-\\dfrac{7}{25}$","$\\dfrac{7}{25},\\dfrac{24}{25}$"],"correct":1,"answer":"$\\sin\\theta=\\sqrt{1-\\dfrac{16}{25}}=\\dfrac{3}{5}$. $\\sin2\\theta=2\\left(\\dfrac{3}{5}\\right)\\left(\\dfrac{4}{5}\\right)=\\dfrac{24}{25}$. $\\cos2\\theta=1-2\\sin^2\\theta=1-\\dfrac{18}{25}=\\dfrac{7}{25}$."}]}]}